    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 29 tests, 0 failures, including the new `Cp18Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for owner creation. When the target city already contains 50 or more owners (compared case-insensitively), the create request is now rejected with **409 Conflict**.\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the household-uniqueness rule), I added:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitive, matching `AssignCustomerCode`'s convention) and throws when the count is \u2265 50. It runs before save, so the count excludes the owner being created.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception carrying the city and count.\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 Conflict`.\n- **`...CityAtCapacityException.yml`** escalation wiring.\n- Wired `checkCityCapacity` into `owners.POST.yml` after `checkHouseholdUnique` and before `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\nThe new `Cp18Tests.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to 50, expects the 51st to 409) passes, and all 29 tests remain green.",
